# Release signing credentials.
#
# Copy this file to key.properties in the same folder and fill it in. That file is
# gitignored and must stay that way: with the keystore and these passwords, anyone can
# publish an update that Android installs over the real app.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generating the keystore (once, on a machine you control)
#
# Without a JDK -- no install needed, prompts for the password so it is never on a command
# line or in a shell history:
#
#     python tools/generate-release-key.py
#
# With a JDK, the equivalent keytool invocation:
#
#     keytool -genkeypair -v \
#       -keystore sma-campus-track.jks \
#       -storetype PKCS12 \
#       -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000 \
#       -alias sma-campus-track \
#       -dname "CN=SMA Campus Track, O=SMA Technology, C=PK"
#
# Both produce the same thing: a PKCS#12 keystore holding one RSA key and a self-signed
# certificate. Run it somewhere sensible -- not C:\Windows\System32, which is where a shell
# opened as administrator starts.
#
# -validity 10000 is about 27 years. A key cannot be swapped later: an app signed with a
# different key is a different app to Android and cannot upgrade the old one in place, so
# every family would have to uninstall and reinstall, losing their session.
#
# BACK THE KEYSTORE UP somewhere durable and private, together with the password. Losing
# either means the app can never be updated again, only replaced under a new application id.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Absolute path is safest: a key outside the working tree cannot be committed by accident.
# On Windows use forward slashes, e.g. C:/Users/you/sma-campus-track-keys/sma-campus-track.jks
storeFile=../../../../sma-campus-track-keys/sma-campus-track.jks

# PKCS12 is what both commands above produce. Set JKS only for an older keystore.
storeType=PKCS12

storePassword=YOUR_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD
keyAlias=sma-campus-track
keyPassword=YOUR_KEY_PASSWORD
